OR","d":"2026-10-29","time":null,"w":7393,"n":114,"url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/portland-general-electric-por-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","lens":{"theater":[0,0,0,0.0],"cinema":[0,0,0,0.0],"imax":[0,0,0,0.0],"streaming":[0,0,0,0.0],"dtc":[0,0,0,0.0],"ai_spend":[0,0,0,0.0],"tariffs":[8,7,1,11.18],"pricing_power":[0,0,0,0.0],"cost_cuts":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0052,"r5":0.0412,"r1_spy":0.0229,"r5_spy":0.0884}}],"quotes":[{"c":"POR 2018 Q2","e":"por","d":"2018-07-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"We actually are already in front of the commission with an example of the sort of thing we're talking about, which is a green tariff to be able to sell 100% green energy to large corporations or other customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/07/30/portland-general-electric-por-q2-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2018 Q3","e":"por","d":"2018-10-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"We continue to work with the commission and interveners on our Green Tariff, a green energy product designed for municipalities and other large customers who want 100% renewable energy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/26/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2018-earn.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2018 Q3","e":"por","d":"2018-10-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"The average customer price increase is expected to be less than 1% with final power cost updates due in mid-November.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/26/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2018-earn.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2018 Q4","e":"por","d":"2019-02-15","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"In addition, we are advancing our green tariff in order to sell 100% renewable energy to our largest commercial and municipal customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/15/portland-general-electric-co-por-q4-2018-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q1","e":"por","d":"2019-04-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"Also in the first quarter, the Public Utility Commission approved our green tariff proposal which we'll bring to market later this spring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/26/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q2","e":"por","d":"2019-08-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"Yeah, Travis, as Maria had pointed out we had a very robust response to phase one of what we call our green tariff.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/05/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q2","e":"por","d":"2019-08-02","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Kevin Wallen","x":"And just the last thing for you, on the green tariff on the phase two, what's the time line for some clarity on whether you guys will be able to invest there or not?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/05/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q2","e":"por","d":"2019-08-02","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"…timing adjustment [Indecipherable] on through, some of these are investments that we pull forward, some of them are onetime items, but we're looking at the balance of the year and remain reiterate our guidance, but we're not providing any additional insight is where we are within that guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/05/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q3","e":"por","d":"2019-11-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"In December, we plan to file the renewable adjustment cost tariff for the Wheatridge Renewable Energy Facility, which is expected to come online in late 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/portland-general-electric-co-por-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q3","e":"por","d":"2019-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"Overall, we're managing costs with the goal of keeping customer price increases at approximately inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/portland-general-electric-co-por-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q4","e":"por","d":"2020-02-14","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"This repurposing is an addition to other cost savings we have been able to achieve in the areas of field productivity, lower generating plant maintenance, IT and financing costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/14/portland-general-electric-co-por-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2019 Q4","e":"por","d":"2020-02-14","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"We've got a lot of cost saving efforts that we've got going on inside the company, they're really showing a lot of promise.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/14/portland-general-electric-co-por-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q1","e":"por","d":"2020-04-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"Our entire management team is taking aggressive actions to reduce operating costs in 2020 and 2021, which will allow us to operate efficiently despite uncertain economic conditions as well as help mitigate further customer price increases and achieve our 2020 revised earnings guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/24/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q1","e":"por","d":"2020-04-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"We have already started taking cost reduction actions and we plan to achieve these savings through implementing a hiring freeze and voluntary furloughs, cutting discretionary expenses, reducing outside services and contract labor and continuing our focus on process improvements and automation…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/24/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q1","e":"por","d":"2020-04-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"…started taking cost reduction actions and we plan to achieve these savings through implementing a hiring freeze and voluntary furloughs, cutting discretionary expenses, reducing outside services and contract labor and continuing our focus on process improvements and automation through the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/24/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q2","e":"por","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"The cost reduction work and focus on O&M is a really important component to us staying in that range for the balance of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q2","e":"por","d":"2020-07-31","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"On our last earnings call, we lowered our guidance to reflect the COVID-19 pandemic and resulting drop in economic activity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q2","e":"por","d":"2020-07-31","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"James Lobdell","x":"Despite this upward revision in demand, we are maintaining guidance due to the structure of the decoupling mechanism.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/portland-general-electric-co-por-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"POR 2020 Q4","e":"por","d":"2021-02-19","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"We are also working to serve many municipal and industrial customers with 100% renewable energy under our green tariff programs, building on our number one decade-long residential clean energy programs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/19/portland-general-electric-co-por-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q1","e":"por","d":"2021-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"So the tax benefit, the $0.11 I mentioned here on the earnings walk bridge is really $0.09 associated with a local pass-through tax that's a one-time adjustment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q1","e":"por","d":"2021-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"So that is really the tax item, a local pass-through tax that should have been booked earlier and over time, very simple, OK.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/portland-general-electric-co-por-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria M. Pope","x":"While we continue to work through the IRP processes this still affords us the opportunity to extend our green community tariff programs and the Transportation Electrification bill that enable us to further support EV adoption, the key infrastructures up to and behind the meter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria M. Pope","x":"We also saw an expansion of the community green tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"…timing of customer bill impacts as well as the impact of COVID-19 on the community, the overall price increase of 3.9% reflects nearly $1 billion of investment to upgrade our system to deliver safe, reliable and clean electricity to customers, specifically our proposed costs for recovery…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria M. Pope","x":"So we worked very hard to keep our price increases as affordable and as low as possible and also to keep the number of issues down.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Maria M. Pope","x":"In addition it cleaned up some language that dates back to restructuring laws from 1999 and some other things like that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"I think, very well for the execution of our strategy for us now to step back and figure out how we want to cost out provide new products and implement -- so we're really pleased by the shape of it, the comprehensive nature of it.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"I will note that even though we have just raised the guidance on O&M, for very good reasons.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q2","e":"por","d":"2021-07-30","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Sophie Karp","x":"And then maybe on guidance and sort of view you're raising guidance and that's great.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/portland-general-electric-company-por-q2-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q3","e":"por","d":"2021-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Brian Russo","x":"And I was wondering if that's captured in the tariff or if that creates the benefit that you potentially retain under the PCAM?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q3","e":"por","d":"2021-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria M. Pope","x":"And if you look at the overall price increases that we have proposed, they're quite modest and it's really hats off to everyone who works at Portland General day in and day out at driving efficiency across our system, better use of technology on digital solutions of putting the customer first in…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q3","e":"por","d":"2021-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Paul Patterson","x":"…cost for customers or, I mean, do you see any of these things as perhaps being-from a sort of a cost reduction perspective, perhaps in terms of delivering this? I mean, in other words, it seemed to me from reading it that they felt that there was some sort of trade off, at least in terms of…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q3","e":"por","d":"2021-10-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"Our year-to-date 2021 performance remains on track and we reaffirm our guidance range of $2.70 to $2.85 and remain on track to achieve long-term earnings growth guidance of 4% to 6% from the 2019 base year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/portland-general-electric-company-por-q3-2021-earn/"},{"c":"POR 2021 Q4","e":"por","d":"2022-02-17","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"Through first, forward pricing updates to the annual update tariff mechanism.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/17/portland-general-electric-por-q4-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"POR 2022 Q1","e":"por","d":"2022-04-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Ajello","x":"The order authorizes a price increase of approximately 3.2% overall.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/04/29/portland-general-electric-por-q1-2022-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"POR 2022 Q1","e":"por","d":"2022-04-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Insoo Kim","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/04/29/portland-general-electric-por-q1-2022-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"POR 2022 Q1","e":"por","d":"2022-04-28","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Ryan Greenwald","x":"Would you guys have reduced guidance if this deferral was excluded in adjusted numbers?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/04/29/portland-general-electric-por-q1-2022-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"POR 2025 Q2","e":"por","d":"2025-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Joe Terpic","x":"We undertook a very similar process in our 2021 RFP, which also navigated tariff and tax policy changes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/05/portland-general-electric-por-earnings-call/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q1","e":"por","d":"2026-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria MacGregor Pope","x":"Importantly, our large load tariff proposal, UM 2377, is in the final stages of review with the OPUC, and we expect an order in the next several weeks.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/portland-general-por-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q1","e":"por","d":"2026-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria MacGregor Pope","x":"A transparent, predictable tariff for new and existing data centers strengthens protections for existing customers while supporting economic development in our region.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/portland-general-por-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q1","e":"por","d":"2026-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joseph R. Trpik","x":"We are confident that these cost savings measures are achievable, especially when considering the $25 million we saved last year, our existing momentum built into our 2026 plan, and the opportunity to accelerate what was planned for 2027 into this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/portland-general-por-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q2","e":"por","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"In Q2, the OPUC issued a final order approving PGE's New Large Load Tariff effective in July, raising average prices approximately 30% for data centers, while lowering rates for all other customers and capping several years of legislative and regulatory work.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/portland-general-electric-por-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q2","e":"por","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"The tariff also creates greater certainty for large load customers by providing a clear pricing framework, which supports investment decisions and continued economic development across our region.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/portland-general-electric-por-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q2","e":"por","d":"2026-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"It's probably too early to speculate, but we're really pleased with the cooperation we had from all of our customers, the partnership with the PUC, the [ legislative ] changes that were made that resulted in a 30% customer price increase for data centers effective in early July.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/portland-general-electric-por-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q2","e":"por","d":"2026-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"…recall, led by the Citizens Utility Board and some others, we worked with parties to come up with something, some legislation in addition to the POWER Act, which resulted in larger customer price increases for data centers, but for not having rate increases go in during certain times of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/portland-general-electric-por-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q3","e":"por","d":"2026-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"Our new large load tariff, effective in July, increased rates for data centers and other large customers while lowering rates for residential and small commercial customers, putting us ahead of many utilities across the country.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/portland-general-electric-por-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"POR 2026 Q3","e":"por","d":"2026-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Maria Pope","x":"The tariff contributed approximately $4 million of incremental margin in the third quarter and includes provisions designed to reduce risk and costs associated with serving new large loads.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/portland-general-electric-por-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[34,1,6288,0,0,0,4190,1673],[35,1,5438,0,0,0,3841,1005],[36,1,4779,0,0,0,3035,1159],[37,1,5435,0,0,0,4153,700],[38,1,5465,0,0,0,3481,1415],[39,1,4241,0,0,0,3530,285],[40,1,5020,0,0,0,3916,646],[41,1,8264,0,0,0,7028,731],[42,1,6037,0,0,0,5417,153],[43,1,5816,0,0,0,4637,757],[44,1,6548,0,0,0,5167,996],[45,1,6301,0,0,0,4992,882],[46,1,8577,0,0,0,6340,1861],[47,1,10771,0,0,0,8457,1791],[48,1,8095,0,0,0,6968,779],[49,1,7909,0,0,0,6099,1273],[50,1,6299,0,0,0,5724,206],[62,1,7446,0,0,0,5606,1318],[65,1,5536,0,0,0,4083,1068],[66,1,5964,0,0,0,4543,1138],[67,1,7393,0,0,0,4999,1716]],"cinema